<div class="docs-pg-layout">
<div class="docs-getstarted-page" style="flex:1;min-width:0;">

  <h1 class="docs-getstarted-title">Getting Started</h1>
  <p class="docs-getstarted-desc">Add SoftUI to your project in seconds. No build tools required.</p>

  <!-- Install -->
  <section class="docs-getstarted-section" id="install">
    <h2>Install</h2>
    <div class="docs-getstarted-code">
<pre><code>npm install softui-css
# or
yarn add softui-css
# or
pnpm add softui-css
# or
bun add softui-css</code></pre>
    </div>
  </section>

  <!-- CDN -->
  <section class="docs-getstarted-section" id="cdn">
    <h2>CDN</h2>
    <p>Drop these two lines into your <code>&lt;head&gt;</code> and you're ready to go:</p>
    <div class="docs-getstarted-code">
<pre><code>&lt;link rel="stylesheet" href="https://unpkg.com/softui-css/dist/softui.min.css"&gt;
&lt;script src="https://unpkg.com/softui-css/dist/softui.min.js"&gt;&lt;/script&gt;</code></pre>
    </div>
    <p style="margin-top:16px;">Optional: load the default fonts (Plus Jakarta Sans and JetBrains Mono). SoftUI doesn't bundle fonts, so without these links it falls back to system fonts. See <a href="/theming/#typography" style="color:var(--sui-primary-text);font-weight:600;">Theming → Typography</a> for self-hosting with Fontsource.</p>
    <div class="docs-getstarted-code">
<pre><code>&lt;link rel="preconnect" href="https://fonts.googleapis.com"&gt;
&lt;link rel="preconnect" href="https://fonts.gstatic.com" crossorigin&gt;
&lt;link href="https://fonts.googleapis.com/css2?family=Plus+Jakarta+Sans:wght@300;400;500;600;700;800&amp;family=JetBrains+Mono:wght@400;500&amp;display=swap" rel="stylesheet"&gt;</code></pre>
    </div>
  </section>

  <!-- JavaScript -->
  <section class="docs-getstarted-section" id="javascript">
    <h2>JavaScript</h2>
    <p>Most components are pure CSS. Some interactive components require <code>softui.js</code> — a dependency-free script{% if bundleSize.js %} (~{{ bundleSize.js.min }} minified, ~{{ bundleSize.js.gzip }} gzipped){% endif %}. Components set themselves up as soon as the DOM is ready; no setup code is needed.</p>
    <p>Include it at the end of your <code>&lt;body&gt;</code>:</p>
    <div class="docs-getstarted-code">
<pre><code>&lt;script src="https://unpkg.com/softui-css/dist/softui.min.js"&gt;&lt;/script&gt;</code></pre>
    </div>
    <p style="margin-top:12px;font-size:14px;color:var(--sui-text-muted);">Components that need JS: Accordion, Calendar, Carousel, Chart, Collapsible, Color Picker, Combobox, Command, Context Menu, Copy Button, Countdown, Data Table, Diff, Dock (magnify effect), Drag &amp; Drop (incl. Kanban), Drawer, Dropdown, Editable Text, File Upload, Image Lightbox, Input OTP, Menubar, Modal, Navigation Menu, Popover, Pricing (selectable), Radial Progress, Rating, Resizable, Scrollspy, Segmented Control, Sheet, Sidebar, Slider, Speed Dial, Styled Select, Swap, Tabs, Text Rotate, Time Picker, Toast, Toggle Group, Tour, Tree View (checkbox propagation), Typewriter, and form enhancements (Password Toggle, Number Input, Tags Input).</p>
  </section>

  <!-- Frameworks -->
  <section class="docs-getstarted-section" id="frameworks">
    <h2>Using with Frameworks</h2>
    <p>SoftUI is plain CSS — it works with any framework. Just import the styles and use the classes.</p>
    <div class="docs-getstarted-code">
<pre><code>/* React — import in your entry file (App.jsx or index.jsx) */
import 'softui-css/dist/softui.min.css';
import 'softui-css/dist/softui.min.js';

function App() {
  return (
    &lt;button className="sui-btn sui-btn-primary"&gt;Click me&lt;/button&gt;
  );
}


/* Vue — import in main.js */
import 'softui-css/dist/softui.min.css';
import 'softui-css/dist/softui.min.js';

&lt;template&gt;
  &lt;button class="sui-btn sui-btn-primary"&gt;Click me&lt;/button&gt;
&lt;/template&gt;


/* Svelte — import in +layout.svelte or app.html */
import 'softui-css/dist/softui.min.css';
import 'softui-css/dist/softui.min.js';

&lt;button class="sui-btn sui-btn-primary"&gt;Click me&lt;/button&gt;


/* Astro — import in your layout */
---
import 'softui-css/dist/softui.min.css';
---
&lt;script src="/node_modules/softui-css/dist/softui.min.js"&gt;&lt;/script&gt;


/* Next.js — import in _app.js or layout.tsx */
import 'softui-css/dist/softui.min.css';
/* Add softui.min.js via Script component or next/script */</code></pre>
    </div>
    <p style="margin-top:12px;font-size:14px;color:var(--sui-text-muted);">Tip: For JS-dependent components (modals, dropdowns, etc.), make sure <code>softui.js</code> loads after the DOM is ready. In React/Vue/Svelte, the import handles this automatically.</p>
  </section>

  <!-- Quick Start -->
  <section class="docs-getstarted-section" id="quickstart">
    <h2>Quick Start</h2>
    <p>Here's a minimal HTML page with a neumorphic button and card:</p>
    <div class="docs-getstarted-code">
<pre><code>&lt;!DOCTYPE html&gt;
&lt;html lang="en"&gt;
&lt;head&gt;
  &lt;meta charset="UTF-8"&gt;
  &lt;meta name="viewport" content="width=device-width, initial-scale=1.0"&gt;
  &lt;link rel="preconnect" href="https://fonts.googleapis.com"&gt;
  &lt;link rel="preconnect" href="https://fonts.gstatic.com" crossorigin&gt;
  &lt;link href="https://fonts.googleapis.com/css2?family=Plus+Jakarta+Sans:wght@300;400;500;600;700;800&amp;family=JetBrains+Mono:wght@400;500&amp;display=swap" rel="stylesheet"&gt;
  &lt;link rel="stylesheet" href="https://unpkg.com/softui-css/dist/softui.min.css"&gt;
&lt;/head&gt;
&lt;body class="sui-d-flex sui-justify-center sui-align-center sui-min-vh-100"&gt;

  &lt;div class="sui-card sui-raised sui-p-5 sui-text-center"&gt;
    &lt;h3&gt;Hello SoftUI&lt;/h3&gt;
    &lt;p class="sui-text-muted sui-mt-2 sui-mb-3"&gt;
      A neumorphic card with a soft raised shadow.
    &lt;/p&gt;
    &lt;button class="sui-btn sui-btn-primary"&gt;Get Started&lt;/button&gt;
  &lt;/div&gt;

  &lt;script src="https://unpkg.com/softui-css/dist/softui.min.js"&gt;&lt;/script&gt;
&lt;/body&gt;
&lt;/html&gt;</code></pre>
    </div>
  </section>

  <!-- Existing Sites -->
  <section class="docs-getstarted-section" id="existing-sites">
    <h2>Using in an Existing Site</h2>
    <p>Neumorphic shadows only work when components sit on the SoftUI background (<code>--sui-bg</code>). SoftUI paints <code>&lt;body&gt;</code> for you, but if your site has its own background, raised and inset shadows will look muddy or disappear.</p>
    <div style="display:flex;gap:16px;flex-wrap:wrap;margin:16px 0;">
      <div data-theme="light" style="flex:1;min-width:180px;background:#fff;color:var(--sui-text);padding:24px;border-radius:var(--sui-radius);border:1px solid var(--sui-bg-dark);">
        <small style="display:block;margin-bottom:12px;color:var(--sui-text-muted);">On a white background</small>
        <div class="sui-card" style="padding:16px;">Raised card</div>
      </div>
      <div class="sui-surface" style="flex:1;min-width:180px;padding:24px;border-radius:var(--sui-radius);border:1px solid var(--sui-bg-dark);">
        <small style="display:block;margin-bottom:12px;color:var(--sui-text-muted);">Inside <code>.sui-surface</code></small>
        <div class="sui-card" style="padding:16px;">Raised card</div>
      </div>
      <div data-theme="light" style="flex:1;min-width:180px;background:#fff;color:var(--sui-text);padding:24px;border-radius:var(--sui-radius);border:1px solid var(--sui-bg-dark);">
        <small style="display:block;margin-bottom:12px;color:var(--sui-text-muted);">With <code>.sui-flat</code></small>
        <div class="sui-card sui-flat" style="padding:16px;">Flat card</div>
      </div>
    </div>
    <p>You have three options:</p>
    <ul style="margin:8px 0 16px 20px;line-height:1.8;">
      <li><strong>Whole page</strong> — let SoftUI style <code>&lt;body&gt;</code> (the default).</li>
      <li><strong>A section</strong> — wrap it in <code>.sui-surface</code> to paint the SoftUI background, text color, and font.</li>
      <li><strong>Individual components</strong> — add <code>.sui-flat</code> to drop the shadow and use a subtle border instead.</li>
    </ul>
    <div class="docs-getstarted-code">
<pre><code>&lt;!-- A SoftUI section inside an existing page --&gt;
&lt;section class="sui-surface sui-p-5"&gt;
  &lt;div class="sui-card"&gt;...&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;/section&gt;

&lt;!-- A dark SoftUI section, even on a light page --&gt;
&lt;section class="sui-surface sui-p-5" data-theme="dark"&gt;
  &lt;div class="sui-card"&gt;...&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;/section&gt;

&lt;!-- A component on your own background --&gt;
&lt;button class="sui-btn sui-flat"&gt;Save&lt;/button&gt;</code></pre>
    </div>
    <p style="margin-top:12px;font-size:14px;color:var(--sui-text-muted);"><code>data-theme</code> works on any element, so you can scope light or dark mode to a single section.</p>
    <p style="margin-top:16px;"><strong>Embed build</strong> (v1.16.0 and later). The standard stylesheet also sets page-wide base styles: a <code>*</code> margin/padding reset, <code>&lt;body&gt;</code> background and font, heading, paragraph, link and <code>code</code> styles, a thin scrollbar, and global reduced-motion and print rules. If you're adding SoftUI to a site that has its own styles, use <code>softui-embed.min.css</code> instead. It has the same components and tokens, but those base styles only apply inside SoftUI elements (anything with a <code>sui-</code> class), so the rest of your page is left alone. That includes utility classes: an element with, say, <code>sui-mt-3</code> or <code>sui-text-center</code> counts as a SoftUI element, so it and its children get SoftUI's reset and typography.</p>
    <div class="docs-getstarted-code">
<pre><code>&lt;link rel="stylesheet" href="https://unpkg.com/softui-css/dist/softui-embed.min.css"&gt;

/* or with a bundler */
import 'softui-css/dist/softui-embed.min.css';</code></pre>
    </div>
    <p style="margin-top:12px;font-size:14px;color:var(--sui-text-muted);">Components still need the SoftUI background for their shadows, so combine the embed build with <code>.sui-surface</code> or <code>.sui-flat</code> as shown above. Use one stylesheet or the other, not both.</p>
  </section>

  <!-- Dark Mode -->
  <section class="docs-getstarted-section" id="darkmode">
    <h2>Dark Mode</h2>
    <p>Add <code>data-theme="dark"</code> to your <code>&lt;html&gt;</code> element. Every component adapts automatically.</p>
    <div class="docs-getstarted-code">
<pre><code>&lt;html data-theme="dark"&gt;</code></pre>
    </div>
    <p style="margin-top:16px;">To prevent a flash of light mode when the page loads, add this blocking script in your <code>&lt;head&gt;</code> before any stylesheets:</p>
    <div class="docs-getstarted-code">
<pre><code>&lt;head&gt;
  &lt;style&gt;body{opacity:0}&lt;/style&gt;
  &lt;script&gt;
    var t = localStorage.getItem('sui-theme');
    if (t === 'dark' || (!t && matchMedia('(prefers-color-scheme:dark)').matches))
      document.documentElement.setAttribute('data-theme', 'dark');
  &lt;/script&gt;
  &lt;link rel="stylesheet" href="softui.min.css"&gt;
&lt;/head&gt;</code></pre>
    </div>
    <p style="margin-top:12px;font-size:14px;color:var(--sui-text-muted);">The inline <code>opacity:0</code> hides the page until SoftUI's CSS loads (which sets <code>opacity:1</code>), eliminating any flash. The script reads the saved theme preference before the first paint.</p>
  </section>

  <!-- Customization -->
  <section class="docs-getstarted-section" id="customize">
    <h2>Customization</h2>
    <p>SoftUI is built on CSS custom properties. Override them anywhere to match your brand:</p>
    <div class="docs-getstarted-code">
<pre><code>:root {
  --sui-primary: #7C5CFC;
  --sui-radius: 12px;
  --sui-shadow-raised: 6px 6px 12px rgba(0,0,0,0.15),
                       -6px -6px 12px rgba(255,255,255,0.05);
}</code></pre>
    </div>
    <p style="margin-top:12px;">See the <a href="/theming/" style="color:var(--sui-primary-text);font-weight:600;">Theming Guide</a> for the full list of variables — colors, shadows, radius, fonts, transitions, and dark mode.</p>
  </section>

  <!-- Browser Support -->
  <section class="docs-getstarted-section" id="browsers">
    <h2>Browser Support</h2>
    <p>SoftUI works in all modern browsers. No polyfills needed.</p>
    <div class="docs-getstarted-code">
<pre><code>Fully Supported:
  Chrome 90+          ✓
  Edge 90+            ✓
  Firefox 100+        ✓
  Safari 15+          ✓
  Opera 76+           ✓

Partial Support:
  Firefox &lt; 121       :has() selector not available (minor styling only)
  Safari &lt; 15.4       backdrop-filter may need -webkit- prefix (already included)
  iOS Safari 15+      ✓ (momentum scrolling included)
  Android Chrome 90+  ✓

Not Supported:
  Internet Explorer   ✗ (uses CSS custom properties, flexbox gap, etc.)</code></pre>
    </div>
    <p style="margin-top:12px;font-size:14px;color:var(--sui-text-muted);">SoftUI uses modern CSS features: custom properties, flexbox gap, <code>:focus-visible</code>, <code>conic-gradient</code>, and <code>prefers-reduced-motion</code>. All vendor prefixes are included where needed.</p>
  </section>

  <!-- RTL Support -->
  <section class="docs-getstarted-section" id="rtl">
    <h2>RTL (Right-to-Left)</h2>
    <p>SoftUI supports right-to-left languages like Arabic, Hebrew, and Farsi. Just add <code>dir="rtl"</code> to your <code>&lt;html&gt;</code> element.</p>
    <div class="docs-getstarted-code">
<pre><code>&lt;html lang="ar" dir="rtl"&gt;</code></pre>
    </div>
    <p style="margin-top:16px;font-size:14px;color:var(--sui-text-muted);">Utility classes (<code>sui-ml-*</code>, <code>sui-mr-*</code>, <code>sui-text-left/right</code>, <code>sui-offset-*</code>) use CSS logical properties and adapt automatically. Components like sheets, carousels, sidebars, breadcrumbs, dropdowns, and tooltips include <code>[dir="rtl"]</code> overrides to flip their positioning.</p>
    <p style="margin-top:12px;"><a href="/rtl-demo/" style="color:var(--sui-primary-text);font-weight:600;">See the full RTL demo &rarr;</a></p>
    <div dir="rtl" lang="ar" style="margin-top:20px;">
      <div class="sui-card sui-raised" style="padding:20px;max-width:400px;">
        <div style="display:flex;align-items:center;gap:12px;margin-bottom:16px;">
          <div class="sui-avatar sui-avatar-sm" style="background:var(--sui-primary);color:#fff;font-weight:600;">م</div>
          <div>
            <div style="font-weight:700;">مرحبا بالعالم</div>
            <div style="font-size:13px;color:var(--sui-text-muted);">هذا مثال على دعم RTL</div>
          </div>
        </div>
        <div class="sui-form-group" style="margin-bottom:12px;">
          <label class="sui-label">البريد الإلكتروني</label>
          <input class="sui-input" type="email" placeholder="example@email.com">
        </div>
        <div style="display:flex;gap:8px;">
          <button class="sui-btn sui-btn-primary">إرسال</button>
          <button class="sui-btn sui-btn-outline">إلغاء</button>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <!-- Print Styles -->
  <section class="docs-getstarted-section" id="print">
    <h2>Print Styles</h2>
    <p>SoftUI includes built-in <code>@media print</code> styles. When users print your page or save as PDF, navbars, sidebars, modals, toasts, and other overlays are automatically hidden. Box-shadows are removed, cards and tables get clean borders, and page breaks are prevented inside components. No extra setup needed.</p>
  </section>

